{{ choice("Improve the view and sound", "Raise the camera to a natural angle, reduce glare and use an existing wired headset if it gives a clearer result.", "#room", "applications", "/img/guides/office-field-guide-v1.webp", "A dock with neatly routed cables.", "Read this part") }}
{{ choice("Run a private test", "Use a preview, test phrase or official test option without recording, sharing sensitive material or inviting another person.", "#test-call", "online", "/img/guides/office-field-guide-v1.webp", "A webcam beside a softly lit desk lamp.", "Read this part") }}
</div></section>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="devices"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Confirm permissions and selections</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Open the video app's settings or preview before the call. Confirm that the intended camera is selected and that the image appears. Select the microphone you expect to use, speak a short test phrase and check the input indicator or test result. Check the selected speaker separately.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the app cannot access a device, review the operating system's permission setting and the app's device selection. Keep the check focused on the chosen app; menus differ between platforms and versions.</p><ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-muted"><li>Check camera access without opening unrelated applications.</li><li>Mute and unmute deliberately so you know which control is active.</li><li>Keep a wired headset you already own as an optional alternative.</li><li>Do not assume a preview confirms future network quality.</li></ul>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="room"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Check the camera view and light</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Place the camera near eye level where practical and look at the whole frame. Check the background for private papers, screens, addresses or other information that should not be visible. Use ordinary daylight or an existing lamp, avoiding strong light directly behind you and glare on your face or screen.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Say the test phrase from your normal seated position. Listen for room echo, fan noise or a blocked microphone. A small change in position can be more useful than adding equipment.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Keep the preview private") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not record the test, share the preview or expose customer, work or personal information while adjusting the background. A clean frame is a privacy check as well as a presentation check.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="test-call"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Run a bounded call check</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use the app's private preview where available. Zoom also provides an optional online test meeting at <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://zoom.us/test">zoom.us/test</a>; follow its prompts and do not invite anyone else. In Zoom's settings, use the audio tests to check the speaker and microphone, then select the device that produced the expected result.</p><div class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto" role="region" aria-label="Home Office Setup reference" tabindex="0"><table role="table" class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base"><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Part</th><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Check</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Part" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Camera</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Your face is visible, the angle is steady and the background is suitable.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Part" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Microphone</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The test phrase registers on the intended microphone without obvious noise.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Part" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Speaker</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The test sound comes from the device you expect to use.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Part" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Light</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Your face is readable without strong glare or backlighting.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Source: <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.zoom.com/hc/en/article?id=zm_kb&sysparm_article=KB0063307">Zoom test meeting guidance</a> and <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.zoom.com/hc/en/article?id=zm_kb&sysparm_article=KB0062765">Zoom audio test guidance</a>.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If calls keep dropping rather than just looking or sounding poor, use the <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-dropouts-diagnosis/">Wi-Fi dropout guide</a> to separate that problem.</p>
